%N A400856 Numbers m such that there exists k such that the multiplicative group of squares modulo k is cyclic of order m.
%C A400856 Write Q(m) = {k : the multiplicative group of squares modulo k is cyclic of order m}, then Q(1) = {k : (Z/kZ)* = (C_2)^r} = {divisors of 24}; for m > 1, k is in Q(m) if and only if (Z/kZ)* is of the form (C_2)^r X C_{2m}.
%C A400856 Factor m = p_1*...*p_s > 1 into prime powers. Then numbers in Q(m) are of the form d*q_{S_1}*...*q_{S_t}, where S_1, ..., S_t is a partition of {1, 2, ..., s}, q_{S_i} is a prime power such that (Z/q_{S_i})* = C_{2*Product_{j in S_i} p_j} or C_2 X C_{2*Product_{j in S_i} p_j}, and d is a divisor of 24 coprime to q_{S_1}*...*q_{S_t}.
%H A400856 Jianing Song, <a href="/A400856/b400856.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
